 policy\"]}]],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex justify-center px-4 md:px-8 mt-6\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"https://dashboard.simpleanalytics.com/?utm_source=vedabase.io&utm_content=badge\",\"referrerPolicy\":\"origin\",\"target\":\"_blank\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"picture\",null,{\"children\":\"$35\"}]}]}]]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"36:T4be,One should be attracted by the beautiful vision of Kṛṣṇa. His name is Kṛṣṇa because He is all-attractive. One who becomes attracted by the beautiful, all-powerful, omnipotent vision of Kṛṣṇa is fortunate. There are different kinds of transcendentalists – some of them are attached to the impersonal Brahman vision, some of them are attracted by the Supersoul feature, etc., but one who is attracted to the personal feature of the Supreme Personality of Godhead, and, above all, one who is attracted by the Supreme Personality of Godhead as Kṛṣṇa Himself, is the most perfect transcendentalist. In other words, devotional service to Kṛṣṇa, in full consciousness, is the most confidential part of knowledge, and this is the essence of the whole Bhagavad-gītā. Karma-yogīs, empiric philosophers, mystics and devotees are all called transcendentalists, but one who is a pure devotee is the best of all. The particular words used here, mā śucaḥ, “Don’t fear, don’t hesitate, don’t worry,” are very significant. One may be perplexed as to how one can give up all kinds of religious forms and simply surrender unto Kṛṣṇa, but such worry is useless.34:[\"$\",\"$L2b\",\"child-4830\",{\"child\":\"$23:props:children:0:props:children:props:page:child_items:4:children:5\",\"hasId\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"em-mb-4 em-leading-8 em-text-base s-justify\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$36\"}}]}]\n"])(function(){function c(){var b=a.contentDocument||(a.contentWindow&&a.contentWindow.document);if(b){var d=b.createElement(''script'');d.innerHTML="window.__CF$cv$params={r:''a3405c0168caf501'',t:''MT